### Step 1: Feature Interaction - Ratio between Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points and Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways
python
# Fire_Roadways_Ratio
# Feature description: The ratio between the distance to fire points and roadways captures how proximity to fire risk and accessibility (e.g., roadways) interacts. Areas closer to roadways may have more human activity, affecting forest type distribution, while areas farther from fire points may be less prone to disturbances.
# Usefulness: This feature could provide insights into how fire and accessibility influence vegetation and forest cover types, which could improve model predictions in forest environments subject to human and natural interactions.
df['Fire_Roadways_Ratio'] = df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points'] / (df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways'] + 1e-6)
end

