# Feature: Distance_To_Human_Impact_Ratio
# Feature description: The ratio between Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways and Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points. This captures the relative influence of human activity (fire ignition vs. roads) in the area.
# Usefulness: A high or low ratio may correlate with proximity to fire-prone or road-accessible areas, distinguishing forest covers impacted by human factors.
df['Distance_To_Human_Impact_Ratio'] = df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways'] / (df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Fire_Points'] + 1e-8)
end

