on\n# Feature name: Terrain_Steepness_Ratio\n# Feature description: Divides 'Slope' by the average Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology and Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways. A combination feature that represents terrain steepness and its proximity to key features like roads and hydrology.\n# Usefulness: Slope steepness combined with distances to hydrology and roadways may capture how accessible or challenging certain terrain is for forest cover types—seed dispersal, water flow, and human activity could vary with this ratio.\ndf['Terrain_Steepness_Ratio'] = df['Slope'] / ((df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology'] + df['Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways']) / 2 + 1e-5)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column Elevation_Hydrology_Diff is dropped\n# The new feature Elevation_RelativeRatio effectively captures the core information from Elevation_Hydrology_Diff in a normalized manner relative to another hydrology-related elevation feature. Thus, this column becomes redundant.\ndf.drop(columns=['Elevation_Hydrology_Diff'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column Hillshade_9am, Hillshade_Noon, and Hillshade_3pm are dropped\n# The aggregation into Combined_Hillshade_Mean provides a simplified yet comprehensive representation of sunlight exposure across the day. Dropping the individual columns prevents excessive dimensionality in the dataset.\ndf.drop(columns=['Hillshade_9am', 'Hillshade_Noon', 'Hillshade_3pm'], inplace=True)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column Wilderness_SOIL32_interaction is dropped\n# This interaction feature has limited variance (many zeros) and is unlikely to contribute significantly to predictions compared to other wilderness-soil interaction terms or aggregated features. Removing it reduces noise in the model.\ndf.drop(columns=['Wilderness_SOIL32_interaction'], inplace=True)\n```end"]
